==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*rōaną||to row}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ere-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*h₁reh₁-||to row}}. Akin to Old Frisian {{term/t|ofs|*roia|*rōia}} (West Frisian {{term|roeie|lang=fy}}), Middle Dutch {{term|royen|lang=dum}} (Dutch {{term|roeien|lang=nl}}), Old Norse {{term|róa|lang=non}} (Danish and Swedish {{term|ro|lang=sv}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈroːwɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=VII|head=rōwan}}

# to [[row]] (with oars etc.)

